  "oracles": [
    "Valid raw packed exchange requests spawn and wait successfully in both SDK builds; the direct build also proves raw direct-register spawn admission.",
    "Malformed headers, counts, string offsets/terminators and insufficient read authority return errors without creating a child; direct scalar/tag/raw-high-word violations are rejected.",
    "128 missing-image failures per arm return only after bootstrap children are reaped, leave no task children and preserve the live parent descriptor count.",
    "waitpid(-1) reaps only recorded native children and leaves an actual unregistered scalar child untouched for the Linux subreaper.",
    "SIGCHLD=SIG_IGN supports 64 spawn/wait ECHILD cycles and 100 further spawns with no intervening wait; detached PID references do not permanently exhaust the 64 slots.",
    "A successfully execed child loses unadmitted inherited fd 199 and rejects ptrace attach. Killing its waiting parent preserves the child, which is adopted and reaped by the Linux subreaper.",
    "32 read-only metadata-count failures per arm terminate the requesting parent with SIGSEGV, and no live or zombie child remains. The supervisor keeps the child input pipe open while checking, so EOF cannot hide a leaked child.",
    "Linux file-nr stays within the fixture tolerance of 16 over its sampled baseline after failed exec and metadata-failure batches; exact after-values are recorded per arm."
  ],
  "scope_exclusions": [
    "Bootstrap-only ptrace rejection and cancellation during a blocked pre-exec bootstrap were not deterministically exercised. The observed ptrace and parent-kill cases are after child exec.",
    "The pinned shell image was staged but not executed; shell syntax/semantics and original SPEC Perl test.pl remain unqualified by this record.",
    "General fork/clone, caller-replacing exec, caught-signal delivery, automatic syscall restart, SMP, multi-threaded domains, arbitrary wait process-group/options and audit/seccomp/tracing remain outside this gate.",
    "Metadata failure is tested through the exchange ABI in both SDK variants. Normal libc posix_spawn also uses the existing packed exchange protocol; explicit direct calls provide direct spawn coverage.",
    "Finite failure and lifetime tests do not prove absence of all races or leaks; delayed cancellation behind uninterruptible filesystem I/O remains unqualified."
  ],
